{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_loopWeightIsHodgeGram'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_loopWeightIsHodgeGram'","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.lean#L72-L78","doc":"**Consistency:** the weakened route reproduces the Gram route's conclusion.\nChaining the implication with `tauRhoHodgeLift_of_realSymm` gives the same B2 lift\nthat `HodgeGramLift.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_loopWeightIsHodgeGram` produces — via the\nstrictly weaker hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.loopWeightIsHodgeGram_imp_realSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.loopWeightIsHodgeGram_imp_realSymm","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.lean#L63-L70","doc":"**The Gram premise is strictly stronger.** `LoopWeightIsHodgeGram` (a Hodge Gram\n`Bᵀ·B`) implies `LoopWeightIsRealSymm` (real symmetric), since `Bᵀ·B` is symmetric\n(`gram_isSymm`). So the positivity carried by the Gram framing is surplus to the B2\nlift's requirement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_realSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_realSymm","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.lean#L54-L61","doc":"**Wall-weakening (sorry-free).** Real + symmetric already instantiates the B2\nlift — positivity is not used. If the loop weight is the complexification of a real\nsymmetric matrix, then `TauRhoHodgeLift` holds for it (with `Wbar = W`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.LoopWeightIsRealSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.LoopWeightIsRealSymm","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LoopWeightRealSymmReduction.lean#L49-L52","doc":"**The minimal B2 premise: the loop weight is real and symmetric.** Strictly\nweaker than `LoopWeightIsHodgeGram` (no positive-semidefiniteness). ","signatureChunk":0}]}